WEBVTT

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:07.080
The Nadesico continues to fight on.

00:00:07.130 --> 00:00:09.800
Whether you like it or not,

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:13.140
the only way to stop all the fighting is to fight on.

00:00:13.670 --> 00:00:15.680
That's what everyone thinks.

00:00:16.130 --> 00:00:20.090
But just how much longer will we have to fight? No one knows.

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:06.660
That dream again.

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:12.700
Echoes of "Self", Echoes of Water

00:02:12.990 --> 00:02:19.170
The Nadesico fights on. Nobody knows when it will all end.

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:34.270
Really, how much longer?

00:02:34.270 --> 00:02:35.230
War

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:41.470
In my spare time, I read about the history of humanity,

00:02:41.470 --> 00:02:44.070
only to find out that most of it is full of war.

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:47.380
Assuming that a person lives for a hundred years,

00:02:47.380 --> 00:02:50.310
does it mean that another ninety years of my life will be filled

00:02:50.310 --> 00:02:52.750
with memories of war like these?

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:56.510
Memories of a time free of war exist for only about ten years,

00:02:56.510 --> 00:02:59.960
before I came aboard the Nadesico. Even then...

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:03.470
Tell me, Omoikane, my memories...

00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:07.930
Since Coming to NADESICO:
You've Asked This Same Question
The Number of Times

00:03:07.930 --> 00:03:10.390
The Same Answer.

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:12.810
I still want to know.

00:03:15.580 --> 00:03:18.250
Seven years ago, Ruri, an unidentified orphan,

00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:22.740
was adopted by a couple who worked at a Nergal subsidiary computing research laboratory.

00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:26.870
Ruri was intellectually nurtured within the laboratory,

00:03:26.870 --> 00:03:32.040
and trained by her foster parents to be a Nadesico crew member, slated to be completed in six years.

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:36.900
In return for a large compensatory award for her education, Ruri was handed over to Nergal.

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:40.570
I remember all that.

00:03:40.570 --> 00:03:42.760
What I want to know is what happened before that.

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:44.170
The Same Answer.

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:45.720
But I still want to know.

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:46.890
Blank.

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:54.820
The answer will never change.
Omoikane doesn't know anything.

00:03:55.240 --> 00:03:56.980
And I can't remember either.

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:00.740
What a fool I am.

00:04:06.510 --> 00:04:06.900
Ruri...

00:04:08.620 --> 00:04:10.130
I am your father.

00:04:11.060 --> 00:04:13.540
Ruri, I am your mother.

00:04:13.860 --> 00:04:15.600
Father... Mother...

00:04:16.870 --> 00:04:20.630
Ruri, I am you first teacher, Archimedes.

00:04:24.260 --> 00:04:25.690
Archimedes.

00:04:26.020 --> 00:04:26.480
Pi.

00:04:29.010 --> 00:04:31.330
Archimedes.

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:32.520
Pi.

00:04:32.780 --> 00:04:36.550
Ruri, I am your father. You did well.

00:04:36.550 --> 00:04:40.240
Ruri, I am your mother. You did well.

00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:43.720
Banzai! Banzai! Banzai!

00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:46.240
Archimedes. Pi!

00:04:46.730 --> 00:04:50.660
Well done, Ruri. You're wonderful, Ruri. You're adorable, Ruri.

00:04:51.070 --> 00:04:53.080
The first words that I learned.

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:56.730
Father, mother, Archimedes, and pi.

00:04:57.600 --> 00:04:59.760
And Pi wasn't apple pie,

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:01.550
but the pi related to the circumference of a circle.

00:05:02.390 --> 00:05:03.250
Goodbye.

00:05:03.660 --> 00:05:05.740
Thanks. Goodbye.

00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:07.680
Next it's time for Japanese.

00:05:08.500 --> 00:05:10.750
I ro ha ni ho he to, chi ri nu ru wo,

00:05:11.090 --> 00:05:12.950
wa ka yo ta re so tsu ne, na ra mu.

00:05:13.330 --> 00:05:14.590
Words beginning with "i".

00:05:14.900 --> 00:05:15.680
Words beginning with "ro".

00:05:16.420 --> 00:05:17.480
Words begin with "ha".

00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:19.060
There sure are a lot words, aren't there?

00:05:19.550 --> 00:05:21.190
Wait a minute, please.

00:05:21.770 --> 00:05:23.220
Yes, what is it, Ruri-san?

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:26.400
What is the meaning of this word?

00:05:27.420 --> 00:05:28.030
Baka?

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:31.850
That is a word that should not be used in everyday life.

00:05:33.130 --> 00:05:33.740
Baka...

00:05:34.240 --> 00:05:37.910
I am your fifth teacher for physics, Einstein.

00:05:38.210 --> 00:05:42.210
Einstein, E equals M C squared.

00:05:42.670 --> 00:05:47.220
Well done, Ruri. You're wonderful, Ruri. You're adorable, Ruri.

00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:49.160
Baka.

00:05:49.930 --> 00:05:52.220
I recall that I did have friends.

00:06:02.750 --> 00:06:05.030
I had human friends as well.

00:06:05.410 --> 00:06:07.510
There were the children I studied with.

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:09.100
We were all alike.

00:06:10.190 --> 00:06:13.970
But our dreams seemed to vary from one to another.

00:06:15.110 --> 00:06:16.840
Father, Mother...

00:06:18.370 --> 00:06:19.710
Papa, Mama...

00:06:20.720 --> 00:06:22.250
You did well.

00:06:50.120 --> 00:06:51.430
That dream again.

00:06:52.330 --> 00:06:53.280
Ruri-chan?

00:06:53.280 --> 00:06:53.780
Yes?

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:56.330
Would you come to the bridge, please?

00:06:56.880 --> 00:06:58.390
Are we under attack?

00:06:58.390 --> 00:07:00.750
No, we have a visitor.

00:07:01.430 --> 00:07:02.610
A visitor?

00:07:03.030 --> 00:07:05.210
Peaceful Dispatch Ambassador Ship
Peaceland

00:07:05.660 --> 00:07:06.500
Peace?

00:07:09.160 --> 00:07:10.840
Peace for peaceful, I suppose.

00:07:11.380 --> 00:07:15.200
Peaceland is a perpetually neutral nation, like Switzerland.

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:17.800
It started out from a theme park where gambling was legal.

00:07:18.180 --> 00:07:22.020
The king, Premier, is the great grandson of the original owner.

00:07:22.020 --> 00:07:24.350
Yes, I remember going there when I was little.

00:07:24.940 --> 00:07:27.200
It's more then a fun place for kids.

00:07:27.200 --> 00:07:29.370
They became independent in the last war,

00:07:29.790 --> 00:07:34.210
and being a nation of legalized gambling and entertainment, the money just keeps rushing in.

00:07:34.490 --> 00:07:39.200
The Peace Bank that was created as an afterthought is now filled with mysterious accounts.

00:07:39.770 --> 00:07:44.750
Everyone wants to hide their extraneous incomes and avoid having to pay taxes.

00:07:45.070 --> 00:07:46.210
Like Nergal?

00:07:46.210 --> 00:07:47.780
In any case,

00:07:47.780 --> 00:07:50.880
the Peace Bank and Swiss banks are known for their absolute secrecy regarding their accounts.

00:07:51.430 --> 00:07:55.460
But who onboard the Nadesico has an account in the Peace Bank?

00:07:55.760 --> 00:07:58.490
Well, they specifically asked for Ruri-san.

00:07:58.490 --> 00:08:00.470
But I don't have any accounts.

00:08:00.800 --> 00:08:03.510
Whatever the case, it's prudent not to anger banks.

00:08:03.510 --> 00:08:06.500
The world revolves around vaults and banks.

00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:08.420
Please be sure to receive them cordially.

00:08:22.240 --> 00:08:23.740
I've come to retrieve you,

00:08:24.050 --> 00:08:24.580
Princess.

00:08:25.460 --> 00:08:26.540
Princess?!

00:08:27.200 --> 00:08:31.670
Your Highness' parents struggled for years to be blessed with children.

00:08:31.870 --> 00:08:35.260
So they attempted to conceive a child through medical means.

00:08:35.780 --> 00:08:38.050
You mean inside a test tube?

00:08:38.570 --> 00:08:40.940
They longed desperately for children.

00:08:41.290 --> 00:08:43.990
But the overseas medical laboratory conducting the work

00:08:43.990 --> 00:08:47.180
was blown apart by terrorists in an unrelated attack.

00:08:47.390 --> 00:08:49.370
Your Highness was lost among the debris,

00:08:49.640 --> 00:08:53.070
and we have been looking for you ever since.

00:08:53.570 --> 00:08:55.280
But I grew up.

00:08:55.670 --> 00:08:57.570
Yes, we are well aware of that.

00:08:57.570 --> 00:08:59.220
And we are absolutely certain as well.

00:08:59.620 --> 00:09:02.950
While other heirs have been born to His Highness since then,

00:09:03.440 --> 00:09:07.120
you are definitely the daughter of the King of Peaceland!

00:09:07.760 --> 00:09:09.940
My biological father and mother...

00:09:11.020 --> 00:09:12.790
Father... Mother...

00:09:17.520 --> 00:09:19.630
A princess?

00:09:21.910 --> 00:09:24.720
Omoikane, give me references on princesses.

00:09:26.560 --> 00:09:29.660
Magical Princess, Natural Lychee!

00:09:31.820 --> 00:09:33.320
Not stuff like that.

00:09:33.710 --> 00:09:35.630
Let me see references besides those related to anime.

00:09:43.570 --> 00:09:45.940
Why? I want to know why?

00:09:46.340 --> 00:09:47.620
We'll be off now.

00:09:47.890 --> 00:09:52.290
Yes, yes. Please watch over her closely, and keep out of trouble.

00:09:53.070 --> 00:09:54.160
I'm a little worried.

00:09:54.480 --> 00:09:56.640
Why? How come?

00:09:57.030 --> 00:10:01.420
This is wartime, so the princess of Peaceland should not travel without a bodyguard.

00:10:01.930 --> 00:10:02.670
But, but...

00:10:03.130 --> 00:10:04.850
Why does it have to be Akito?!

00:10:05.510 --> 00:10:06.980
So why me?

00:10:06.980 --> 00:10:11.230
I understand that no princess is supposed to be without a knight.

00:10:11.590 --> 00:10:12.390
Oh, really?

00:10:13.080 --> 00:10:14.730
How did you find out about things like that?

00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:16.330
I watched some videos.

00:10:35.870 --> 00:10:38.340
Hark! Ruri is the name, is it not?

00:10:38.560 --> 00:10:41.680
My dear child, thank the Heavens!

00:10:42.280 --> 00:10:43.930
Are you my father?

00:10:44.610 --> 00:10:47.060
Yes, I am your father!

00:10:47.820 --> 00:10:49.280
And this is your mother!

00:10:49.280 --> 00:10:52.140
Oh dear, oh dear, you have grown up to be such a wonderful girl!

00:10:52.340 --> 00:10:54.060
And...

00:10:54.260 --> 00:10:56.290
These are your brothers!

00:10:57.650 --> 00:11:01.240
Welcome, Ruri-san, our dear onee-sama.

00:11:04.490 --> 00:11:05.570
This isn't the place.

00:11:05.810 --> 00:11:08.200
We are all together now.

00:11:08.660 --> 00:11:10.660
You can be with us all you want, dearest.

00:11:13.500 --> 00:11:15.500
Father, I have a request.

00:11:15.800 --> 00:11:17.890
Make any wish, child.

00:11:18.490 --> 00:11:19.300
Time...

00:11:19.810 --> 00:11:21.240
I would like some time.

00:11:38.620 --> 00:11:40.570
How much more, Ruri-chan?

00:11:41.040 --> 00:11:44.570
Spanners for Seiya-san, spices for Houmei-san,

00:11:44.940 --> 00:11:46.490
a teddy bear for Inez-san.

00:11:57.090 --> 00:11:59.050
Whoa!

00:12:00.130 --> 00:12:02.960
O Solo Mio!

00:12:02.960 --> 00:12:05.730
Our authentic house specialty five star Peaceland original,

00:12:05.730 --> 00:12:06.800
pizza and pasta!

00:12:07.390 --> 00:12:10.380
Peaceland original? But pasta and pizza are from...

00:12:10.380 --> 00:12:11.970
From Naples, Italy.

00:12:13.310 --> 00:12:15.560
Everything in this country has been borrowed from elsewhere.

00:12:16.270 --> 00:12:17.270
Hey, little girl,

00:12:17.270 --> 00:12:19.350
Would you mind saying that after you've tried what's being offered?

00:12:19.820 --> 00:12:21.400
See for yourself what this is like!

00:12:21.980 --> 00:12:22.490
Okay.

00:12:25.250 --> 00:12:27.530
So, what do you think of our house specialty pizza?

00:12:30.820 --> 00:12:33.560
Well, I grew up on Mars, so I can't say for sure, but...

00:12:33.560 --> 00:12:34.300
Tastes bad.

00:12:36.050 --> 00:12:37.100
It tastes bad.

00:12:37.440 --> 00:12:38.670
Tastes disgusting, in fact.

00:12:39.400 --> 00:12:40.840
What was that?!

00:12:41.440 --> 00:12:42.610
Ruri? Ruri-chan?

00:12:42.610 --> 00:12:48.060
Excessive amounts of spices, black spices and peppers, with cheese and olive oil all of mediocre quality.

00:12:48.060 --> 00:12:51.210
Cooking that simply attempts to over-stimulate the tongue

00:12:51.210 --> 00:12:53.610
is something that's expected from a third-rate cook.

00:12:53.610 --> 00:12:57.060
A Martian and a brat are going to insult my cooking?

00:12:57.430 --> 00:13:00.800
It doesn't matter if the person is from Mars or Jupiter,

00:13:00.800 --> 00:13:03.730
any human being would find this pizza and pasta terrible.

00:13:04.110 --> 00:13:06.650
Any person who would enjoy this must have damaged taste buds.

00:13:07.030 --> 00:13:08.680
You're interfering with my business.

00:13:08.680 --> 00:13:09.560
I'll throw you out!

00:13:09.560 --> 00:13:11.950
Stop it! Don't touch this girl!

00:13:17.230 --> 00:13:17.950
Tenkawa-san!

00:13:23.590 --> 00:13:25.510
That should be enough to teach you a lesson.

00:13:31.870 --> 00:13:32.720
Master!

00:13:32.720 --> 00:13:33.330
Boss!

00:13:33.330 --> 00:13:34.100
Chief!

00:13:34.100 --> 00:13:34.770
Teacher!

00:13:34.980 --> 00:13:37.180
You've got some nerve, you little runt!

00:13:37.560 --> 00:13:39.730
He was the one who threw the first punch.

00:13:39.890 --> 00:13:41.210
I don't care!

00:13:41.210 --> 00:13:43.690
Stay away from her! You'll settle this with me!

00:13:43.970 --> 00:13:47.130
Trying to be her knight in shining armor?
You got some balls!

00:13:47.130 --> 00:13:49.330
She's not some princess!
Who the hell do you think you are?

00:13:55.030 --> 00:13:57.000
I come all the way out here just to get into a fight.

00:13:57.700 --> 00:13:59.460
Peaceland? Yeah, right.

00:14:01.370 --> 00:14:03.940
I'm sorry. It was my fault.

00:14:04.460 --> 00:14:07.950
Protecting the princess is the knight's job, right?

00:14:08.650 --> 00:14:11.510
Of course, I can't say much for myself, getting beaten into a pulp.

00:14:13.570 --> 00:14:15.010
That sure was some rancid tasting pizza, wasn't it?

00:14:15.010 --> 00:14:17.260
It's hard to believe it came from this world.

00:14:21.390 --> 00:14:25.070
A fjord in Scandinavia?
Why are we going to such a place?

00:14:25.070 --> 00:14:26.400
I asked my father.

00:14:27.090 --> 00:14:28.550
If I have biological parents,

00:14:28.550 --> 00:14:30.440
then there must be adoptive parents.

00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:32.780
But I can't remember.

00:14:40.160 --> 00:14:41.370
Jeez.

00:14:49.690 --> 00:14:50.380
Ruri-chan?

00:15:47.360 --> 00:15:48.540
You must be Ruri-san.

00:15:51.730 --> 00:15:55.280
A messenger from the King informed me that you would be coming.

00:15:56.580 --> 00:15:57.660
Are you ...

00:15:58.270 --> 00:15:58.740
my father?

00:15:59.020 --> 00:15:59.840
Father?

00:16:00.360 --> 00:16:03.370
Father... I suppose so.

00:16:04.270 --> 00:16:07.920
That day, numerous unidentifiable fertilized eggs in test tubes

00:16:07.920 --> 00:16:11.600
were brought in from the medical facility that had been bombed.

00:16:11.600 --> 00:16:14.090
Most of them were already dead.

00:16:14.460 --> 00:16:19.190
But we felt that those that survived had the right to live,

00:16:19.530 --> 00:16:21.310
even if that meant becoming test subjects.

00:16:22.270 --> 00:16:23.290
Test subjects?

00:16:23.620 --> 00:16:27.810
People can defeat cancer by altering a few genes.

00:16:28.840 --> 00:16:32.590
Genetic manipulation is such an outdated way of thinking.

00:16:32.970 --> 00:16:36.150
But humanity's future lay on that path.

00:16:36.670 --> 00:16:39.070
Superb intelligence that could adapt to future science.

00:16:39.590 --> 00:16:40.990
A body free of disease.

00:16:41.490 --> 00:16:47.820
Genetic manipulation is the only way to make humans who can withstand the challenges of interstellar travel.

00:16:48.840 --> 00:16:52.460
Here, the air is clean, the water untainted.

00:16:52.570 --> 00:16:54.300
Ozone depletion is not pronounced.

00:16:54.580 --> 00:16:57.710
A place perfect to raise such children.

00:16:58.330 --> 00:17:01.430
Here we instituted infant education.

00:17:01.480 --> 00:17:05.300
The children sucked in knowledge like cotton soaking in moisture.

00:17:05.300 --> 00:17:07.220
Their genes were altered, weren't they?

00:17:07.530 --> 00:17:10.270
Humans learn too many unnecessary things.

00:17:10.890 --> 00:17:14.040
We only taught our children what they needed to know.

00:17:14.040 --> 00:17:16.330
We did not waste brain capacity.

00:17:16.690 --> 00:17:19.200
You are the testimony to all of this, Ruri-san.

00:17:19.440 --> 00:17:23.160
At your young age, for all practical purposes, you control the Nadesico.

00:17:23.450 --> 00:17:26.610
Clearly you are superior to other human beings.

00:17:27.060 --> 00:17:29.410
I am proud of what you've become.

00:17:29.990 --> 00:17:32.110
And the other children?

00:17:32.830 --> 00:17:35.040
It's very tragic, but failures do happen.

00:17:35.500 --> 00:17:38.410
This methodology was banned years ago.

00:17:38.720 --> 00:17:40.910
You see what has become of the institute.

00:17:41.880 --> 00:17:46.200
But Ruri-san, you are one of the few successes to have come out of this.

00:17:47.050 --> 00:17:50.650
Of course, now that you know you are a princess,

00:17:50.650 --> 00:17:52.530
your happiness may lie elsewhere.

00:17:53.690 --> 00:17:55.100
I must return this to you.

00:17:56.890 --> 00:18:02.130
When you were four, a Nergal-linked organization recruited you and your left this place.

00:18:02.130 --> 00:18:05.310
I deposited the money I received in a savings account for you,

00:18:05.310 --> 00:18:06.540
just in case something happened.

00:18:06.820 --> 00:18:10.660
With that card, you will be able to withdraw money from an account in Peace Bank.

00:18:11.310 --> 00:18:12.460
About my father and mother...

00:18:14.130 --> 00:18:16.250
Is this what you had in mind?

00:18:19.060 --> 00:18:21.940
Ruri, I am your father.

00:18:21.940 --> 00:18:24.300
Ruri, I am your mother.

00:18:27.010 --> 00:18:31.100
Well done, Ruri. You're wonderful, Ruri. You're adorable, Ruri.

00:18:32.120 --> 00:18:34.350
Children need parents.

00:18:37.750 --> 00:18:40.990
Good parents that never scold their children.

00:18:41.500 --> 00:18:44.030
Normal people could never fit the bill.

00:18:52.200 --> 00:18:54.210
Thank you for letting me live.

00:18:56.050 --> 00:18:57.380
It was nothing extraordinary.

00:18:58.260 --> 00:19:01.220
But nobody asked you to do something like this.

00:19:08.190 --> 00:19:10.560
Please go ahead and use this.

00:19:19.430 --> 00:19:20.030
Baka.

00:19:43.700 --> 00:19:44.430
Ruri-chan!

00:19:45.130 --> 00:19:46.890
That sound... That's the sound.

00:20:13.820 --> 00:20:14.870
Wow.

00:20:16.020 --> 00:20:17.200
Schools of salmon.

00:20:23.440 --> 00:20:25.800
I've never seen real ones before.

00:20:30.480 --> 00:20:35.400
I returned to the Nadesico with her complement of BAKA-bakka, in the end.

00:21:49.140 --> 00:21:50.800
Just like Lindbergh,

00:21:50.800 --> 00:21:54.410
high flying pilots, in love with the stars in the moonlit twilight.

00:21:55.450 --> 00:21:59.170
I've come a long ways since those dreams I had in my childhood.

00:21:59.820 --> 00:22:01.860
To be told I'm but a fool would make my sky blue eyes

00:22:01.860 --> 00:22:03.270
change to eyes the color of the oceans.

00:22:04.720 --> 00:22:06.530
The next episode of Martian Successor Nadesico is:

00:22:07.040 --> 00:22:08.830
"You're the Next Captain of the Nadesico!"

00:22:09.250 --> 00:22:10.620
Look forward to this one, alright?
